# WORKING COPY — Safari attachment upload (single Blob PUT)

**Status:** Verified working on staging after Cloudflare **HTTP/3 (QUIC) was turned Off** for the `privatenote.ai` zone. Do **not** reintroduce HTTP chunking for this path.

## App recipe (shipped)

| Requirement | Value |
|---|---|
| Staging page | `https://premium.privatenote.ai` |
| Staging upload | `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |
| Prod page | `https://privatenote.ai` |
| Prod upload | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` |
| Transport | **XHR** `xhr.send(Blob)` (never Safari `fetch` for the binary PUT) |
| Body | one Blob `{ type: "application/octet-stream" }` |
| Method | PUT `/api/notes/:id/file` |
| Auth | **`Authorization: Bearer {uploadToken}`** (primary); query `?uploadToken=` fallback |
| Headers | Do **not** set `Content-Type` / `Content-Length` from JS for Blob PUTs |
| Credentials | omit / `withCredentials` false |
| Proxy | never Pages `/api` for the binary body |
| Worker | Stream single-blob body to R2 (no full `arrayBuffer()` buffer) |
| Chunking | `SAFARI_CHUNKING_ENABLED = false` |

## CORS (upload relay)

Echo Origin, echo `Access-Control-Request-Headers`, Allow-Methods GET/POST/PUT/OPTIONS, Max-Age 86400, allow `Authorization` + `Content-Length`, **no** Allow-Credentials, **no** Set-Cookie.

## REQUIRED Cloudflare fix (root cause of ~200 ms Safari status 0)

**Symptom:** Safari ~30 MiB XHR PUT → `status: 0` / “network connection was lost” in ~150–300 ms; no Worker log. curl 31 MiB PUT to the same host succeeded. Bearer vs query both failed identically. OPTIONS/CORS were fine.

**Cause:** Safari preferred **HTTP/3 (QUIC)** (`Alt-Svc: h3=":443"`). Large browser PUTs on that path aborted before the Worker. HTTP/2 was fine.

**Fix (confirmed working):**

1. Cloudflare Dashboard → zone **`privatenote.ai`**
2. **Speed** → **Settings** (or Optimization) → **Protocol Optimization**
3. **HTTP/3 (with QUIC)** → **Off**
4. Retest in a Private Window (Safari caches `Alt-Svc`)

**Preferred long-term (keep H3 for the rest of the site):** Response Header Transform Rule removing `Alt-Svc` for:

- `upload-staging.privatenote.ai`
- `upload.privatenote.ai`

Match: `(http.host eq "upload-staging.privatenote.ai") or (http.host eq "upload.privatenote.ai")` → Remove header `Alt-Svc`.

If large Safari PUTs regress with ~200 ms `status: 0` and no Worker log again, check HTTP/3 / `Alt-Svc` on the upload hosts first — not chunking, not Bearer.
